---
---
<section class="usecases-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">What you can build</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">From factory floor to cloud, in JavaScript.</h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle">
        node-opcua powers the application and integration layer of industrial systems.
        Here's what teams ship with it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="usecases-grid">
      <div class="usecase-card">
        <div class="usecase-icon">⇄</div>
        <h3 class="usecase-title">Protocol gateways</h3>
        <p class="usecase-body">
          Bridge S7, Modbus, MQTT, BACnet, or proprietary protocols to OPC UA.
          Bidirectional, with buffering and reconnect logic built in.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="usecase-card">
        <div class="usecase-icon">◎</div>
        <h3 class="usecase-title">OPC UA servers for your devices</h3>
        <p class="usecase-body">
          Expose your machine's data model as a standards-compliant OPC UA address space.
          Companion specs (Euromap, PackML, LADS) supported.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="usecase-card">
        <div class="usecase-icon">▲</div>
        <h3 class="usecase-title">Edge data collectors</h3>
        <p class="usecase-body">
          Subscribe to hundreds of variables across multiple PLCs. Aggregate,
          filter, and forward to your historian, time-series DB, or cloud platform.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="usecase-card">
        <div class="usecase-icon">☁</div>
        <h3 class="usecase-title">Cloud &amp; IoT bridges</h3>
        <p class="usecase-body">
          Connect OPC UA to AWS IoT Greengrass, Azure IoT Hub, Google Cloud IoT,
          or any MQTT/REST backend. node-opcua runs where Node.js runs.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="usecase-card">
        <div class="usecase-icon">⬡</div>
        <h3 class="usecase-title">MES &amp; ERP connectors</h3>
        <p class="usecase-body">
          Read production data from the shop floor and push it to SAP, Oracle,
          or your custom MES. Real-time, with type-safe mappings.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="usecase-card">
        <div class="usecase-icon">◉</div>
        <h3 class="usecase-title">Node-RED OPC UA nodes</h3>
        <p class="usecase-body">
          The official OPC UA nodes for Node-RED are built on node-opcua.
          Low-code OPC UA integration used by thousands of flows worldwide.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .usecases-section {
    padding: var(--space-section) 0;
    background-color: var(--bg);
  }
  .section-header {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 650px;
    margin: 0 auto 3.5rem auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
  .section-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.25rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }
  .section-subtitle {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .usecases-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 2rem;
    max-width: 1000px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .usecase-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.625rem;
    padding: 1.75rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--divider);
  }
  .usecase-icon {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
  .usecase-title {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }
  .usecase-body {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 48ch;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .usecases-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
      column-gap: 3rem;
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .usecases-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      column-gap: 3rem;
    }
  }
</style>
